---
import Title from "@components/global/Title.astro";
---

<section>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-8 py-12 md:px-12 lg:px-32 lg:py-32">
		<div>
			<Title title="Terms & Conditions" subtitle="Last updated 5 September 2026" class="pb-10 pt-20 uppercase" />
		</div>
		<div class="prose-styles mt-12 lg:mt-24">
			<p>
				These terms cover the web design and development services provided by caleb.rocks — the freelance service operated by
				<strong>Caleb Bruce Whittaker, sole trader (ABN 62 866 297 258)</strong>, based on the Granite Belt, Queensland, Australia ("I", "me",
				"my"). By engaging my services you agree to them. They're written to be read, not decoded.
			</p>

			<h2>Quotes and scope</h2>
			<p>
				Every project starts with a free chat and a written quote. Quotes are valid for 30 days and state the agreed scope — pages, features, and
				what's included in the chosen package (Essential or Signature). Work outside the agreed scope is quoted separately before it's done, so
				there are no surprises on the invoice.
			</p>

			<h2>Accepting a project</h2>
			<p>
				A project begins when you accept the written quote or proposal and the required deposit has been received. The quote, agreed scope and
				these terms together form the agreement for the project. If there is any conflict, the written quote or proposal takes priority for
				project-specific details.
			</p>

			<h2>Payment</h2>
			<p>
				Projects are invoiced in Australian dollars; invoices will state any applicable GST. Payment is 50% deposit before work begins and 50%
				after final approval, before the site goes live. The final domain cutover and launch don't happen until the final payment is received.
				Domain registration and other third-party costs are billed at cost. Bank transfer is the usual payment method.
			</p>
			<p>
				Website Care is A$69/month (or A$199/quarter), billed in advance, and can be cancelled anytime — it runs to the end of the paid month. Work
				outside a package or Care plan is charged at A$95/hour in 30-minute increments, or quoted for larger pieces.
			</p>

			<h2>Cancellation</h2>
			<p>
				You can cancel a project at any time by letting me know in writing. If you cancel after work has begun, amounts already paid may be
				retained to cover work completed, time reserved and reasonable costs incurred up to the date of cancellation. If the value of work
				completed exceeds the amount already paid, I may invoice the difference. Any amount paid for work that has not been performed or costs
				that have not been incurred will be dealt with in accordance with applicable law.
			</p>

			<h2>Client delays and inactive projects</h2>
			<p>
				Project timelines rely on you providing content, access and feedback when reasonably requested. Delays on your side may move the delivery
				date. If a project is inactive for more than 30 days because required material or feedback has not been provided, I may pause the project
				and reschedule the remaining work. If it remains inactive for more than 60 days, I may close the project and invoice for work completed to
				that point. Restarting a closed project may require a new timeline or quote.
			</p>

			<h2>Revisions</h2>
			<p>
				Each package includes the revision rounds stated on the pricing page (two for Essential, three for Signature). A revision round is
				consolidated feedback on the current design — not a new direction. Beyond the included rounds, extra revisions are charged at the hourly
				rate or quoted before proceeding.
			</p>

			<h2>Timelines</h2>
			<p>
				Timelines are agreed in the quote and depend on photos, content and feedback arriving when promised. If something on your side delays
				things, no stress — the timeline just shifts accordingly, and I'll keep you posted.
			</p>

			<h2>Your content and responsibilities</h2>
			<p>
				You are responsible for checking the accuracy, legality and suitability of information you provide or approve, including names, prices,
				claims, licences, opening hours, photographs and contact details. You confirm that you have the necessary rights or permission to use
				content you supply. I may flag apparent issues, but I am not responsible for independently verifying your business claims or legal
				compliance unless specifically agreed.
			</p>

			<h2>Concept redesigns</h2>
			<p>
				The concept redesigns shown on this site are speculative works I created to demonstrate my standard of work. They are not client
				commissions, and the businesses named have not necessarily engaged me. Pre-engagement concept work remains my intellectual property until
				a project is agreed and paid for.
			</p>

			<h2>Who owns what</h2>
			<p>
				Once all project invoices are paid in full, you receive ownership of the client-specific content and original design work created
				specifically for your project, together with the right to use the finished website for your business. I retain ownership of my
				pre-existing code, reusable components, development methods, templates, utilities and general know-how. Third-party software, fonts,
				images, libraries and other licensed materials remain subject to their original licences. Where reusable or third-party material forms
				part of the finished site, you receive the rights necessary to use it as part of that website. I may display the finished work in my
				portfolio unless we agree otherwise in writing.
			</p>

			<h2>Third-party services</h2>
			<p>
				Websites may rely on third-party services such as domain registrars, hosting providers, email services, form processors, analytics
				platforms, map providers or other integrations. Those services operate under their own terms, pricing and availability. I will take
				reasonable care when configuring them, but I do not control and cannot guarantee the continued availability, pricing, compatibility or
				performance of third-party services.
			</p>

			<h2>Warranties and liability</h2>
			<p>
				I provide services with reasonable care and skill. Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any right, guarantee or remedy
				that cannot lawfully be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law or other applicable law. Subject to those rights, I am not responsible
				for loss caused by matters outside my reasonable control, including third-party outages, unauthorised changes made by others, compromised
				client accounts, domain or email provider failures, or use of the website in a way it was not designed for. To the extent permitted by law,
				I am not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential loss.
			</p>

			<h2>Search engines and business results</h2>
			<p>
				Where SEO foundations, Search Console or similar services are included, I will implement the agreed technical and on-page work with
				reasonable care. I do not guarantee search rankings, traffic levels, enquiries, sales or any other particular business result, as these
				depend on factors outside my control.
			</p>

			<h2>Browser and device compatibility</h2>
			<p>
				Websites are tested against current mainstream browsers and common screen sizes at the time of delivery. I do not guarantee identical
				appearance or functionality on obsolete browsers, unsupported devices or future software versions.
			</p>

			<h2>Domains, accounts and backups</h2>
			<p>
				Wherever practical, domains and business-critical third-party accounts remain in your ownership and control. You are responsible for
				maintaining access to your domain registrar, email and other accounts after handover. I may retain working copies or backups for a
				reasonable period, but unless a separate maintenance or backup service is agreed, I do not promise indefinite storage of project files or
				website backups.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
			<p>
				If these terms change, the date at the top of this page changes with them. The terms that apply to a project are the ones current when the
				quote was accepted.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:hello@caleb.rocks">hello@caleb.rocks</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
